d say that you're moving towards  that the far right or you actually  courting the far right how would you  address that criticism all right let me  address it this way for the last 25  years and myself and everybody a new kid  has worked to restore our country's  former status as an independent  democratic nation that's governed by our  politicians elected by us seqable by us  in accordance with our traditional laws  and customs and constitution now if that  makes you far right then I think whoever  thinks that has got a very strange idea  about what constitutes far white  far-right politics having always been a  democratic party bringing Tommy Robinson  into UK well first of all that's  something that isn't going to happen in  the near future the rules would have to  be changed to allow that to happen as  I'm on record of saying I think that  that is something that I personally  would approve of but it's a matter for  the party it's their decision it's not  mine it's I'm not a dictator and I'm  going to gauge the mood of the party on  that as I mingle around today I'll be  very busy over the next two days talking  to many of those thousand people who are  coming and see how they feel about it it  was the Democratic football lads  Alliance that their Facebook page  criticized for racist rants continuously  and you spoke on on their platform a  platform after which arrests were made  yes and that is that I'm glad you give  them raised that because you give me an  opportunity to comment on the absolute  disgraceful coverage of that by Sky News  when you portrayed that as an  anti-muslim rally it what let me let me  be the one pissed about to tell you  because it wasn't an anti-muslim rally  it was a rally on behalf of justice for  women and children victims of sexual  abuse that I went along to talk because  they invited me the DFL I actually  organized the rally and the people who  caused the violence at that at that  meeting we've had a chance to  investigate that 